API = Application Programming Interface

An API is a defined interface/contract that allows one software application or service to interact with another.

Application A
      ↓
     API
      ↓
Application B

The API defines how the interaction should happen and what kind of request/response is expected.

Web API:
Uses a network protocol such as HTTP/HTTPS.
GET https://api.example.com/users/123

Non-web API:

Doesn't use HTTP/HTTPS. It can be an interface provided by:
Programming libraries
Operating systems
SDKs
example:
Java Application
      ↓
Java Library API
      ↓
Library function


| Method     | Typical purpose  |
| ---------- | ---------------- |
| **GET**    | Retrieve data    |
| **POST**   | Create/send data |
| **PUT**    | Replace/update   |
| **PATCH**  | Partially update |
| **DELETE** | Delete           |

